Why not dfs?DFS (Depth-First Search) goes as deep as possible before backtracking. This can easily cause it to find longer cycles first, because it doesn’t explore in increasing order of path length.DFS can detect if a cycle exists but it cannot ensure that the first cycle found is the shortest one.
